  "//peerDependencies": [
    "REQUIRED: @hotwired/stimulus (70 shipped files import it), @hotwired/turbo-rails (used as the",
    "  window.Turbo global, never imported -- so a bundler will not tell you it is missing),",
    "  and daisyui, because the components emit daisyUI class names from Ruby: without it they",
    "  render unstyled, not merely unthemed.",
    "EVERYTHING ELSE IS OPTIONAL. Bali is a component library and no app uses all of it; each",
    "  optional peer is listed next to the entry that reaches for it.",
    "  Root entry, per controller: @glidejs/glide (carousel), @googlemaps/markerclusterer +",
    "  @rails/activestorage (locations map, direct upload), @rails/request.js, date-fns",
    "  (timeago), flatpickr (datepicker), lodash.debounce, lodash.throttle, rrule (recurrent",
    "  event rule), slim-select, sortablejs (kanban, sortable list), tippy.js.",
    "  ./charts: chart.js.",
    "  ./block-editor: @blocknote/core + /react + /mantine, @mantine/core, @mantine/hooks,",
    "    react, react-dom -- all MPL-2.0 or MIT. `shiki` is only needed for syntax-highlighted",
    "    code blocks; pass syntax_highlighting: false and you can skip it.",
    "    The @blocknote/* lower bound is 0.52.1 because that is the version spec/dummy pins and",
    "    the one the editor was exercised against by hand. It is not an aspiration: do not widen",
    "    it downwards without running the editor on the version you want to claim.",
    "  ./react-island: none -- it only imports @hotwired/stimulus. An island SUBCLASS loads react",
    "    and react-dom (>=18) inside loadComponent(), so they stay attributed to the island's own",
    "    entry and optional for apps without islands (see docs/api/react-island.md).",
    "  ./rich-text-editor: the @tiptap/* set plus lowlight, highlight.js. DEPRECATED in v3 and",
    "    removed in v4 -- migrate to ./block-editor.",
    "DELIBERATELY ABSENT -- @blocknote/xl-ai, xl-multi-column, xl-pdf-exporter, xl-docx-exporter",
    "  and their companions (`ai`, `docx`, `@react-pdf/renderer`). Those four are",
    "  'GPL-3.0 OR PROPRIETARY': a closed-source application needs a paid commercial licence.",
    "  Declaring them as peers led people to install them by reflex. They are documented in",
    "  docs/api/block-editor.md, and the loader keeps them lazy so an app that never turns those",
    "  features on still builds and runs without them."
  ],
